; `RELATION` and `NAME` index by *character name*: Emuera builds a reverse
; dictionary from every chara template's Name, Callname and Nickname to that
; template's `No` (`GameData/ConstantData.cs:690-700`) and hands it to
; `VariableCode.RELATION` with `allowIndex 1` and `VariableCode.NAME` with
; `allowIndex -1`, both reporting `chara*.csv` as the error position
; (`:1061-1070`). First definition wins.
;
; The template here is `CSV/CHARA3.CSV` — `番号,3` / `名前,이름` — so the name
; `이름` must resolve to 3 wherever a RELATION target index is expected.
@SYSTEM_TITLE
ADDCHARA 3

; written through the name, read back through the number
RELATION:0:이름 = 7
PRINTFORML byname={RELATION:0:3}

; and the other way round
RELATION:0:3 = 11
PRINTFORML bynumber={RELATION:0:이름}

; the name is an ordinary index expression, so it composes
PRINTFORML sum={RELATION:0:이름 + 0}
